ation\"><br>Other compounds halide can't be removed because corresponding C<sup>+</sup> is highly unstable."},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"निम्नलिखित यौगिकों I-IV में से, कौन सा एक (i) NaOH (ii) पतला HNO<sub>3</sub> (iii) AgNO<sub>3</sub> के साथ क्रमिक प्रतिक्रिया करने पर एक पीली अवक्षेप बनाता है?<br><br><picture><source media=\"(max-width: 320px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktciamvh/980b6e24-e75b-4ffd-a45a-3ed3320eebf6/0e2f3fd0-1131-11ec-a8f2-7da4f0f15eab/file-1ktciamvi-320w.jpg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 500px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktciamvh/980b6e24-e75b-4ffd-a45a-3ed3320eebf6/0e2f3fd0-1131-11ec-a8f2-7da4f0f15eab/file-1ktciamvi-500w.jpg\"><source media=\"(max-width: 680px)\" srcset=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktciamvh/980b6e24-e75b-4ffd-a45a-3ed3320eebf6/0e2f3fd0-1131-11ec-a8f2-7da4f0f15eab/file-1ktciamvi-680w.jpg\"><img src=\"https://imagex.cdn.examgoal.net/1ktciamvh/980b6e24-e75b-4ffd-a45a-3ed3320eebf6/0e2f3fd0-1131-11ec-a8f2-7da4f0f15eab/file-1ktciamvi.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;height: auto;display: block;margin: 0 auto;\" loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Morning Shift Chemistry - Haloalkanes and Haloarenes Question 107 Hindi\"></picture>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"II"},{"identifier":"B","content":"IV"},{"identifier":"C","content":"I"},{"identifier":"D","content":"III"}],"correct_options":["B"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"haloarenes","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-26th-august-morning-shift","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":[],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-26th-august-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"1ktb5a0k2","chapter":"structure-of-atom","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Morning Shift","permalink":"given-below-are-two-statementsbrbrstatement-i--accor-jee-main-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-hxunvfvm2q5vue7l","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"Given below are two statements.<br><br>Statement I : According to Bohr's model of an atom, qualitatively the magnitude of velocity of electron increases with decrease in positive charges on the nucleus as there is no strong hold on the electron by the nucleus.<br><br>Statement II : According to Bohr's model of an atom, qualitatively the magnitude of velocity of electron increases with decrease in principal quantum number.<br><br>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are false"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are true"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Statement I is false but Statement II is true"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement I is true but Statement II is false"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"Velocity of electron in Bohr's atom is given by <br><br><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.798ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"6.909ex\" height=\"2.782ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -877 3053.8 1229.7\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D449\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D449\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(1046.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"221D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-221D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"TeXAtom\" data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\" transform=\"translate(2102.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mfrac\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(220,394) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D44D\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44D\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(263.5,-345) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D45B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D45B\"></use></g><rect width=\"711.2\" height=\"60\" x=\"120\" y=\"220\"></rect></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container><br><br>Z = atomic number of atom, corresponds to +ve charge so as Z increase velocity increases so statement I is wrong and as 'n' decreases velocity increases so statement II is correct."},"hi":{"direction":null,"content":"नीचे दो कथन दिए गए हैं।<br><br>कथन I : एक परमाणु के बोहर मॉडल के अनुसार, मात्रात्मक रूप से इलेक्ट्रॉन की गति नाभिक पर सकारात्मक आवेशों में कमी के साथ बढ़ती है क्योंकि नाभिक द्वारा इलेक्ट्रॉन पर मजबूत पकड़ नहीं होती है।<br><br>कथन II : एक परमाणु के बोहर मॉडल के अनुसार, मात्रात्मक रूप से इलेक्ट्रॉन की गति मुख्य क्वांटम संख्या में कमी के साथ बढ़ती है।<br><br>उपरोक्त कथनों के प्रकाश में, नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से सबसे उपयुक्त उत्तर चुनें :","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"कथन I और कथन II दोनों गलत हैं"},{"identifier":"B","content":"कथन I और कथन II दोनों सही हैं"},{"identifier":"C","content":"कथन I गलत है लेकिन कथन II सही है"},{"identifier":"D","content":"कथन I सही है लेकिन कथन II गलत है"}],"correct_options":["C"],"answer":null,"explanation":null,"comprehension":null}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"bohrs-model-for-hydrogen-atom","type":"mcq","year":2021,"paperId":"jee-main-2021-online-26th-august-morning-shift","isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2021-online-26th-august-morning-shift","active":true},{"question_id":"1ktb5fie5","chapter":"aldehydes-ketones-and-carboxylic-acids","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperTitle":"JEE Main 2021 (Online) 26th August Morning Shift","permalink":"the-correct-sequential-addition-of-reagents-in-the-preparati-jee-